{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-5564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $P(7,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(7,4)$ means the same thing as ${}_{7}{P}_{4}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(7,4) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =840.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c448d18e7c9bc818e92f8a5364e735a7abb8b17cd3b9945a96010c5e9f2062c"} {"question" "q-5564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "140"] ["math" "210"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "840"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "840"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Cheryl holds a bag of $40$ marbles, each one with a slightly different size or color. If she picks $5$ of them out one at a time and lines up in a row, how many different lines of $5$ marbles are possible?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $40$ marbles to choose from, so $n=40.$ We want to select $5$ of those marbles for the line, so we have $r=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to line up $5$ marbles is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{40}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{40!}{(40-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40!}{35!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38\\cdot 37\\cdot 36\\cdot \\cancel{35!}}{\\cancel{35!}} \\\\  & =40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38\\cdot 37\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =78\\,960\\,960.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c448d18e7c9bc818e92f8a5364e735a7abb8b17cd3b9945a96010c5e9f2062c"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120\\,450"] ["math" "24\\,670\\,820"] ["math" "4\\,320\\,560"] ["math" "780\\,560"] ["math" "78\\,960\\,960"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-5570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "78\\,960\\,960"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Victoria has the $4$ playing cards: the ace of clubs, the ace of diamonds, the ace of hearts, and the ace of spades. She takes one card and places it in front of her. She then does the same with another card. In how many different ways can she choose a sequence of $2$ cards like this?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $4$ cards, so $n=4.$ We want to select $2$ of those cards to make a sequence of $2$ cards, so we have $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to choose the cards is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{4}{P}_{2} & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4!}{2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{\\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c448d18e7c9bc818e92f8a5364e735a7abb8b17cd3b9945a96010c5e9f2062c"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-84982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$P(45,0)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(45,0)$ means the same thing as ${}_{45}{P}_{0}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(45,0) & =\\frac{45!}{(45-0)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{45!}}{\\cancel{45!}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c448d18e7c9bc818e92f8a5364e735a7abb8b17cd3b9945a96010c5e9f2062c"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "45"] ["math" "450"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-85048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-122479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Erik has an encyclopedia with $24$ tomes and is selecting $3$ tomes to read first, second, and third. How many different choices does Erik have?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-122479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$ tomes to choose from, so $n=24.$ We want to select $3$ of those tomes for Erik to read, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices Erik has is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{24}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{24!}{(24-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24!}{21!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22\\cdot \\cancel{21!}}{\\cancel{21!}} \\\\  & =24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =12\\,144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881ec74f188"} {"question" "q-122479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0c448d18e7c9bc818e92f8a5364e735a7abb8b17cd3b9945a96010c5e9f2062c"} {"question" "q-122479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037884/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe920c22295b2fdf54c982ddc7ca43bbfe531968afb685d9ebf1881e